      "score": 9,
      "comments": 13,
      "author": "Yogthos",
      "published": "2026-10-24T14:18:48Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Developing simulations on 16 MHz chips requires fixed-point arithmetic and strict cycle budgeting to bypass absent hardware floating-point units.",
        "Severe RAM constraints demand aggressive bit-packing, lean data structures, and streaming map tiles directly from flash or external storage.",
        "Playable rendering relies on dirty-rectangle updates, minimal framebuffers, and spreading cellular-automata simulation ticks across multiple display frames."
      ]
    },
